-- title:
--   Existence of a chart table of ideal sheaves on Resolution(t,e)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, let $t \in W$ and let $e$ be a natural number, and assume that the quotient ring $W/(t)$ is reduced. Write $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t$ for the $W$-algebra $W[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - t)$, i.e. the quotient of `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) W` by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(t)$, and let `Resolution t e` be the scheme obtained as the colimit of the diagram `glueDiagram t e` on the index category `GlueIndex e`, whose values are the charts `glueObj t e` and whose maps are the gluing morphisms. The assertion is that there exists a family $F : \mathrm{Fin}(e+1) \to$ `(Resolution t e).IdealSheafData` of ideal-sheaf data on this scheme such that for every chart index $i : \mathrm{Fin}\,e$ and every $k : \mathrm{Fin}(e+1)$ the pullback $(F_k)$`.comap (ι t e i)` along the $i$-th chart morphism `ι t e i` is the ideal sheaf `ofIdealTop` attached to the global ideal obtained by transporting, along the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso` for `CommRingCat.of (CrossingQuotient W t)`, the ideal of $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t$ equal to the principal ideal generated by `V t` when $k = i$, to the principal ideal generated by `U t` when $k = i+1$, and to the unit ideal $\top$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the existence form of the "chart table" for the $e+1$ reduced components of the special fibre of the toric resolution of $uv = t^e$: each $F_k$ cuts out, in the $i$-th chart $\operatorname{Spec}(W[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-t))$, the divisor $(V t)$ for $k=i$, the divisor $(U t)$ for $k = i+1$, and nothing otherwise. It packages the chart computation in the hypothesis shape consumed downstream, where the resulting invertibility and divisor identities feed the construction of resolved models of modular curves.
